godzilla vs kong is finally out in the  world and while most people are paying  attention to the eponymous titans the  film has more than just these two  monsters  here are five characters from the film  who are more important than you probably  realize  in the last few years podcasts and  podcasters have increasingly grown in  popularity and as the volume of podcasts  increases so too does the number of  podcasters becoming household names  it seems safe to say that by the end of  godzilla vs kong bernie hayes  played by brian tyree henry is about to  become the most famous podcaster in the  world of kaiju  by the time we're introduced to bernie  he's already dedicated several hundred  episodes worth of podcast time to  exploring the conspiracies behind  monarch and giant monsters  if bernie's podcast was popular before  the events of godzilla vs kong then  imagine how popular he'll be after  playing an active role in helping the  two monsters defeat mecha godzilla  and imagine how informed the public at  large will be about apex and their  shenanigans  and while we're on the subject of giant  robots  there aren't exactly villains in  godzilla versus kong so much as there  are antagonists who think they're doing  something smart  only to wind up hoisted by their own  egomania ren serizawa played by shuna  guri  is one half of a duo of bad guys whose  belief is very simple  in order for humanity to thrive they  must prove themselves to be a stronger  collective apex predator than any giant  monster  the creation of mechagodzilla using the  combined mind of king ghidorah's brain  and the human mind may have failed but  that doesn't mean it will be the last  effort made toward a similar end  and while ren seems pretty dead by the  end of godzilla vs kong that doesn't  mean his story is over  we can always see a prequel story  explaining how ren came to create mecha  godzilla  ren is after all the son of ken  watanabe's ishiro serizawa who has much  more of the opinion that humanity should  play its part in the world by sometimes  standing back and letting the giant  monsters fight  [Music]  let them fight what caused ren to employ  a decidedly opposing tactic not to  restate things but godzilla vs kong is  primarily focused on the stories of two  giant monsters  however nathan lind played by alexander  skarsgard has a backstory way too  important not to flesh out later  when lin is approached by walter simmons  about his potential involvement in  traveling to the center of hollow earth  we get a very brief mention of his past  attempt  what we know is that lin's brother died  in an attempt to get to the kaiju  stomping grounds but we don't really  know how that happened  we don't know why lind is fixated on  hollow earth we don't know how he became  affiliated with monarch and we didn't  see him fall out with the organization  either  that story is at least worth a tie-in  comic but much like ren the other reason  why lind is so important is that it's  his ideas that helped drive the journey  to hollow earth in the first place  it seems likely that lind will play an  important role in understanding and even  benefiting from hollow earth and  forthcoming stories  eileen andrews played by rebecca hall is  the reason king kong stays safe for as  long as he does  she's his guardian in many ways the  containment area kong calls home  exists in part because of andrews and  the safeguards used to keep kong safe as  he travels to hollow earth are a result  of her care as well  when we see hollow earth one of the  things we notice straight away is that  there is even more monster life down  there  and if there is anyone who can catalog  and understand that life it's eileen  andrews  andrews is important for the future of  this franchise precisely because she'll  likely stand opposed to the  destroy all monsters edict of the  antagonists and as she takes on more  power and monarch in the wake of the  story and he attempts to build max will  likely be tempered by andrew's level  head and respect for all of nature's  creatures  including kong all that being said there  is one character in godzilla versus kong  who stands head and shoulders above the  entire rest of the cast  gia played by kaylee hoddle to say that  gia's empathy and ability to communicate  with kong literally saved all of  humanity's collective bacon  is probably an understatement and she's  only going to become more important for  humans and monsters alike both  as she gets older if you recall in kong  skull island the island is home to more  than just the big eight  there's also a tribe of people living  symbiotically with him and while kong  protects those people they also respect  and watch out for him  we find out in godzilla vs kong that the  only surviving member of that tribe is  jia and it's through her ability to use  sign language that humanity learns kong  isn't just  intelligent but also able to communicate  jiya is so in tune with kong that she  can feel his heart slow down to the  point of death  without her he wouldn't even be alive  right now it's hard to say that there's  anyone else who could convince kong to  fight for the human race at this point  other than gia similarly we may discover  that other monsters are able to  communicate through sign language  as she gets older it seems likely that  gia may not only be the person best able  to understand these creatures  she may also be their strongest advocate  check out one of our newest videos right  here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite movie moments are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

